# vendor/images/ is never referenced by a COPY/ADD in any Dockerfile --
# it's loaded into Docker's image store via `docker load`
# (tools/offlinebuild, tools/vendorimages), a separate mechanism from the
# build context entirely. Excluding its ~390MB here speeds up every
# `docker build` in this repo, since Docker otherwise sends the whole
# context to the daemon up front regardless of what a Dockerfile actually
# uses.
vendor/images/

.git/
